; Test two boxes for overlap
;
; Entry point of #R$A600, #R$A822 and #R$B665 (which load IX themselves): the overlap test. Compares the box (D,
; E)..(B, C) with the player box #R$8516 (min x, max x, min y, max y of Jean) and jumps to IX with carry set when they
; overlap, clear when not.
;
; D Top of the box (y)
; E Left of the box (x)
; B Bottom of the box (y)
; C Right of the box (x)
; IX Where to go on (carry set: overlap)
@label=OverlapTest
c$A85F LD HL,($8516) ; H = player min x, L = player max x
 $A862 LD A,B        ; entity max x below the player min x: no
 $A863 CP H          ;
 $A864 JR C,$A877    ; no
 $A866 LD A,D        ; entity min x not below the player max x: no
 $A867 CP L          ;
 $A868 JR NC,$A877   ; no
 $A86A LD HL,($8518) ; H = player min y, L = player max y
 $A86D LD A,C        ; entity max y below the player min y: no
 $A86E CP H          ;
 $A86F JR C,$A877    ; no
 $A871 LD A,E        ; entity min y not below the player max y: no
 $A872 CP L          ;
 $A873 JR NC,$A877   ; no
 $A875 JP (IX)       ; overlap: carry is set by the last CP
*$A877 OR A          ; no overlap: carry clear
 $A878 JP (IX)       ;
